codex
The root cause is now evidenced: this container’s PID namespace reports small process IDs, while `/proc/<pid>` is from a different namespace. Lean 4.22 looks up `/proc/<its-pid>/exe`, gets `ENOENT`, and aborts; `/proc/self/exe` works. I’m applying a narrowly scoped compatibility preload that redirects only `/proc/<digits>/exe` reads to `/proc/self/exe`, then rerunning the pinned tools unchanged.
